ck your inbox."},"errors":{"invalidCredentials":"Wrong email or password.","invalidPseudoCredentials":"Wrong username or password.","emailAlreadyExists":"An account already exists with this email address.","pseudoTaken":"This username is already taken. Choose another one.","emailNotConfirmed":"Your email address has not been confirmed yet. Check your inbox.","rateLimit":"Too many attempts. Please wait a few minutes before trying again.","weakPassword":"Password too weak. Use at least 8 characters.","invalidEmail":"Invalid email address.","network":"Cannot reach the server. Check your connection.","signInFailed":"Sign-in failed. Check your credentials.","signUpFailed":"Account creation failed. Please try again.","wrongPassword":"Incorrect password.","repatriationFailed":"Could not move your cloud projects to this browser. Your account has not been deleted.","deleteAccountFailed":"Account deletion failed. Please try again."},"cloudAccount":{"title":"Cloud account","projectCount":"{count, plural, one {# project in the cloud} other {# projects in the cloud}}","projectCountLoading":"Loading projects…","openProject":"Open a project","signOut":"Sign out","deleteAccount":"Delete my account"},"deleteAccount":{"title":"Delete my account","warning":"This cannot be undone: your account, your profile and your training progress will be deleted. The share links of your projects will stop working.","repatriation":"{count, plural, one {Your cloud project will be moved} other {Your # cloud projects will be moved}} to this browser before the deletion.","noCloudProjects":"Your local projects are not affected.","passwordLabel":"Confirm with your password","confirm":"Delete permanently","cancel":"Cancel","deleted":"Your account has been deleted."}},"profile":{"prompt":{"userTypeTitle":"You use Studomate as a…","userTypeHint":"Optional, to help us understand who uses the app.","schoolTypeTitle":"One last question","schoolTypeQuestion":"What kind of school do you study in?","skip":"Skip"},"fields":{"userType":"You use Studomate as a","schoolType":"Type of school","notProvided":"Not provided"},"userTypes":{"student":"Student","teacher":"Teacher / trainer","professional":"Automation professional","self_learner":"Self-learner / curious","other":"Other"},"schoolTypes":{"high_school":"High school","bts":"BTS (vocational post-secondary)","iut":"IUT / BUT (university institute of technology)","university":"University","engineering_school":"Engineering school","other":"Other"}},"whatsNew":{"title":"What's new in Studomate {version}","previous":"Previous","next":"Next","done":"Got it","slides":{"grafcetEditor":{"title":"The GRAFCET editor gets smarter","body":"Drop or move a step, a transition, an action or a step referral next to a compatible element: the link is created for you and the element snaps into place. When you move a step or a transition, its aligned actions and step referrals follow it."},"actionChains":{"title":"Chain the actions of a step","body":"An action now has a connection point on its right: link it to the next action to build a step → action → action chain. A new action chains itself after the previous one, and a moved action takes the rest of its chain along. If you delete the step, the chain stays together: link its first action to another step to reattach everything."},"scene3dDisplay":{"title":"Show the 3D scene where you want","body":"Show the 3D scene in a panel on the right of the editors, to follow the grafcet and the operative part side by side, for example when projecting. You can also open it in a floating box that you move and resize like a window, in a page of the editor or in a browser tab. The View menu and the \"3D scene\" button of the status bar open the scene in the chosen mode."}}}},"now":"$undefined","timeZone":"UTC","children":["$L1a","$L1b"]}]
18:["$","$L19",null,{"formats":"$undefined","locale":"en","messages":{"public":{"landing":{"heroTitle":"Learn GRAFCET and Ladder<br></br>by simulating them","heroTagline":"Design, simulate and test your automation logic with animated HMIs, right in your browser.","heroBadges":"Free and open source · No install · No account · No personal data","heroSceneLabel":"3D animation of a box-sorting station: a conveyor brings each box and cylinders sort it by height.","followTraining":"Take the course","showcaseGrafcetAlt":"The Studomate editor simulating a GRAFCET","showcaseLadderAlt":"The Studomate editor simulating a Ladder diagram","showcaseHmiAlt":"The Studomate HMI editor","demoTitle":"See Studomate in action","demoVideoLabel":"Demo of building and simulating a project with Studomate","demoVideoPause":"Pause the demo","demoVideoPlay":"Play the demo","logicTitle":"Write the logic","logicIntro":"GRAFCET and Ladder in the same project, sharing the same variables.","machineTitle":"Drive the machine","machineIntro":"Connect your program to an HMI, a 3D scene or a real Arduino board.","showcaseGrafcetTitle":"GRAFCET","showcaseGrafcetText":"Draw steps, transitions and branches, then follow the GRAFCET as it runs: active steps, true conditions, running actions.","showcaseLadderTitle":"Ladder","showcaseLadderText":"Build rungs with contacts, coils, timers and counters, and watch power flow through them during simulation.","showcaseHmiTitle":"HMI","showcaseHmiText":"Build animated supervision pages (lights, buttons, tanks, moving objects) wired to the same variables as your programs.","showcaseScene3dTitle":"3D scenes","showcaseScene3dText":"Connect your program to a virtual 3D plant (conveyors, cylinders, sensors) and watch the machine respond in real time.","showcaseScene3dAlt":"3D scene of a box-sorting station driven by Studomate","showcaseArduinoTitle":"Arduino","showcaseArduinoText":"Load your program onto a real Arduino Uno R3 board, or use its inputs and outputs during simulation, straight from Chrome or Edge.","showcaseArduinoAlt":"Arduino Uno R3 board","whyTitle":"Why Studomate?","whyIntro":"Studomate exists to cut the friction of learning automation down to almost nothing.","reasonFrictionTitle":"Zero friction","reasonFrictionText":"No install, no licence, no PLC or I/O cards to set up. You focus on the logic, not the tool.","reasonAllInOneTitle":"All-in-one","reasonAllInOneText":"GRAFCET, Ladder and animated HMIs in the same environment, with variables shared across all three. No free tool combines the three.","reasonShortLoopTitle":"Short correction loop","reasonShortLoopText":"Errors are flagged while you edit, not only when you start the simulation. A fast, visual right to make mistakes.","audienceStudents":"Students (technical colleges, engineering schools, universities)","audienceTeachers":"Teachers and trainers in automation / electrical engineering","audienceProfessionals":"Professionals retraining or brushing up","featureSimulationTitle":"Real-time simulation","featureSimulationText":"Step-by-step or continuous execution, with live visualisation of states, transitions and variables.","featureManualTitle":"Built-in manual","featureManualText":"Complete help available straight from the app.","featureCloudTitle":"Accounts & cloud (optional)","featureCloudText":"Projects stored locally or in the cloud, with link sharing.","stepsTitle":"Get started in 30 seconds","step1Title":"Open the app","step1Text":"Nothing to install — it all runs in the browser.","step2Title":"Create a project or start from an example","step2Text":"Start from scratch or open one of the ready-made templates.","step3Title":"Analyse, then simulate","step3Text":"Check the structure, then run the logic and watch the system react.","trainingTitle":"Learn industrial automation with Studomate","trainingIntro":"Guided modules to master GRAFCET, then Ladder, with exercises you can simulate in the app.","trainingA0LinkLabel":"Automation basics","trainingA0Topic":"Basics","trainingA0Summary":"Automation, variables, basic logic and the scan cycle.","trainingA1LinkLabel":"GRAFCET basics","trainingA1Topic":"GRAFCET","trainingA1Summary":"Steps, transitions, actions, OR and AND branches.","trainingA2LinkLabel":"Ladder logic and memory","trainingA2Topic":"Ladder","trainingA2Summary":"Contacts, coils, latching, set/reset coils and edges.","trainingA3LinkLabel":"Ladder timers, counters and calculation","trainingA3Topic":"Ladder","trainingA3Summary":"Timers, counters, calculations and subroutines.","trainingA4LinkLabel":"From GRAFCET to ladder logic (part 1)","trainingA4Topic":"GRAFCET → Ladder","trainingA4Summary":"Implement a GRAFCET in Ladder: one network per transition, two programs, actions, time and faults.","trainingA5LinkLabel":"From GRAFCET to ladder logic (part 2)","trainingA5Topic":"GRAFCET → Ladder (continued)","trainingA5Summary":"OR and AND divergences, stopping a sequence, limits of one network per transition and the three-block method.","trainingCta":"Browse all training","templatesTitle":"Examples to get you started","templatesIntro":"Open a pre-configured project and explore it at your own pace.","templatePreviewAlt":"Preview of the {label} project","openInApp":"Open in the app","durabilityTitle":"Your projects are yours","durabilityNoLockInTitle":"No lock-in","durabilityNoLockInText":"Your projects are files you export and keep. The schema is versioned: a project exported today will still open after the tool is updated.","durabilityIndependenceTitle":"You depend on no one","durabilityIndependenceText":"The code is free under the AGPL v3 licence: if the project stops, it can be forked or self-hosted.","privacyTitle":"Built for privacy","privacyText":"No email required, no personal data stored, no tracking cookies. Authentication uses a nickname, and usage statistics are anonymous.","sourceCodeText":"The source code is public: read it, report an issue or contribute.","viewOnGitHub":"View on GitHub","openApp":"Open the app"}},"templates":{"traffic-light":{"label":"Traffic light","description":"3 boolean outputs (red, amber, green) + an HMI with coloured indicators. To be programmed."},"crossroads":{"label":"Traffic light crossroads","description":"12 boolean outputs (red/amber/green × 4 lights: NS1, NS2, EO1, EO2) + an HMI with the crossroads. Plant simulated by the 3D scene. To be programmed."},"drilling":{"label":"Drilling station","description":"Sequential cycle driven by limit switches: start button, lowering, timed drilling, raising. Console and plant simulated by the 3D scene. To be programmed."},"elevator":{"label":"Lift","description":"3-floor lift: landing and car buttons, floor display and lamps in the 3D scene that simulates the plant. To be programmed."},"parking":{"label":"Barrier car park","description":"Two barriers (entry and exit) and a space counter: sensors for a waiting car, a photocell under the barrier, a \"full\" lamp and a counter in the 3D scene, where the Arrival and Departure buttons bring cars. To be programmed."},"carton-sorting":{"label":"Carton sorting station","description":"Sorting cartons by height: detection at the post, routing by three cylinders to two output conveyors, counting. Plant simulated by the 3D scene. To be programmed."},"linear-sequence":{"label":"Linear sequence","description":"A 4-step GRAFCET, a single chain, no timer or divergence. Training module mini-exercise."},"and-divergence":{"label":"AND divergence","description":"An AND divergence closed by its convergence, two parallel branches. Training module mini-exercise."},"or-divergence":{"label":"OR divergence","description":"A two-branch OR divergence with mutually exclusive branches, each looping back to the initial state on its own. Training module mini-exercise."},"timer-cycle":{"label":"Timer","description":"A 2-step GRAFCET alternating on two timers, no input. Training module observation."},"ladder-and-or":{"label":"Series and parallel contacts","description":"Two networks provided: toggle a and b in simulation to observe AND and OR. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-reading":{"label":"Read a Ladder program","description":"Four combinational networks provided: predict the outputs, then check in simulation. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-logic":{"label":"Two-way lighting","description":"Combinational logic: two switches and an enable. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-self-holding":{"label":"Pump: self-holding","description":"Push-button start, stop priority, self-holding. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-interlock":{"label":"Reversing motor","description":"Two interlocked self-holdings with a common stop. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-memory":{"label":"Pump: latched fault","description":"Thermal relay, latched fault lamp, acknowledgement without automatic restart. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-edges-reading":{"label":"Read edges","description":"The same input on a NO, P and N contact: record the timing diagram. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-toggle":{"label":"Impulse relay","description":"One button turns a lamp on then off: network execution order and P contact. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-gate":{"label":"Motorised gate","description":"Two interlocked directions, limit switches, stop, photocell. The student declares the inputs. Training module synthesis."},"ladder-timers-reading":{"label":"Read timers","description":"A TON, a TOF and a TP on the same input: draw the timing diagrams. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-timers":{"label":"Star-delta start","description":"Star then delta with a TON, fan held by a TOF, two-TON blinker. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-counters":{"label":"Counting","description":"Piece counting (CTU), buffer zone (CTUD), stock (CTD). Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-tank":{"label":"Tank","description":"Level hysteresis, alarm, start counter on a P contact. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-scaling":{"label":"Scaling","description":"Computing a level from a raw value: overflow, truncation, REAL computation. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-subprograms":{"label":"Subprograms","description":"Call the counting subprogram from the Main, and see the effect of a conditional call. Training module mini-exercise."},"ladder-packing":{"label":"Case packing","description":"Conveyor, fault, counting and box change in subprograms. No variables provided. Training module synthesis."},"linear-sequence-naive-ladder":{"label":"Linear sequence: textbook method","description":"Linear GRAFCET implemented with one self-holding per step: observe the overlap. Training module mini-exercise."},"linear-sequence-ladder":{"label":"Linear sequence in Ladder","description":"Implement a linear GRAFCET in Ladder, one network per transition. Training module mini-exercise."},"drilling-ladder":{"label":"Drilling station in Ladder","description":"Drilling GRAFCET in Ladder, timer and descent watchdog. Training module synthesis."},"or-divergence-ladder":{"label":"OR divergence in Ladder","description":"An OR divergence implemented in Ladder. Training module mini-exercise."},"and-divergence-ladder":{"label":"AND divergence in Ladder","description":"An AND divergence implemented in Ladder. Training module mini-exercise."},"traffic-light-ladder":{"label":"Traffic light in Ladder","description":"Traffic light in Ladder with reset and end-of-cycle stop. Training module mini-exercise."},"parking-ladder":{"label":"Parking in Ladder","description":"Parking control in Ladder, signalling provided, reset. Training module synthesis."},"gate-per-transition-ladder":{"label":"Remote-controlled gate: one network per transition","description":"Single-button gate implemented with one network per transition. Training module example."},"gate-grafcet-ladder":{"label":"Remote-controlled gate: three blocks","description":"Single-button gate implemented in three blocks. Training module example."}}},"now":"$undefined","timeZone":"UTC","children":"$L1c"}]
